{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat collab/yang-clojure/1794210000000-architect-cc1-p1-confirm.findings.md && cat .agents/skills/code-review-pr/references/review_checklist.md && sed -n '1,220p' .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py\"","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT / Completed-Local: 2026-11-09 07:37 GMT / 2026-11-09 14:37 +0700\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES — P1-1 remains open; P1-2 is corrected.**\n\n1. **P1-1: recovery can attach another occurrence’s origin.** At [macro.cljc:693](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:693), `lineage-origin-for` returns the first candidate matching either rows-vector identity **or elementwise row identity**. Distinct occurrences of identical content share row objects because [packet-of:110](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:110) retrieves them from the same index. An earlier candidate’s elementwise match therefore wins before the actual source packet’s exact match.\n\n   Static reproduction:\n\n   ```clojure\n   (defmacro pick-second [a b]\n     (conj [] (first b) (first (rest b))))\n   (defmacro feed [x]\n     (yin/application (yin/variable 'pick-second)\n       [x (yin/application (yin/variable 'f) [(yin/literal 1)])]))\n   (defn f [y] y)\n   (feed (f 1))\n   ```\n\n   `pick-second` receives equal-content operands with different histories: `a` retains the source admission; `b` belongs to the `feed` expansion. Both contain identical row objects. Reassembling `b` recovers **`a`’s source origin**, so its correspondence incorrectly records `[:retained source-admission]` instead of `[:retained feed-expansion-origin]`. Child insertion propagates that same incorrect recovery.\n\n   The original single-operand pins are addressed, but the minimum correction requires preserving the **correct occurrence’s** provenance. Prefer exact container lineage and eliminate first-match selection among ambiguous row-level matches; propagate occurrence-specific lineage or explicitly refuse ambiguity. Add this nested, equal-content/different-origin case.\n\n2. **P1-2: minimum correction met.** [strip-tracking:635](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:635) recursively removes only `:yin.vm.macro/origin-of` from supported payload collections and metadata, preserving legitimate metadata entries. [construct:760](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:760) applies it to `:data`/`:key` slots before hashing. The `packet-data` pin covers the original encoding failure.\n\nReviewed the worktree patch over `fa70516f`, read-only. No tests were run; the reported Node/JVM 28 tests and 257 assertions do not cover the remaining collision above.# Code Review PR Checklist & Taxonomy\n\nWhen performing code reviews, evaluate changes using this structured checklist and severity taxonomy.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Finding Severity Taxonomy\n\n| Severity | Label | Definition | Examples |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **P0** | **Critical (Blocker)** | Security vulnerabilities, data loss risks, production crashes, secret leakage. Must be fixed before merging. | Hardcoded tokens, unhandled NullPointer on critical path, SQL injection, broken auth check. |\n| **P1** | **High (Must Address)** | Logic bugs, breaking API changes, missing error handling on external calls, race conditions, lack of tests for complex logic. | Swallowed exceptions, broken retry loop, missing backward compatibility in API schema. |\n| **P2** | **Medium (Recommended)** | Performance inefficiencies, code duplication, sub-optimal data structures, non-idiomatic style. | Unnecessary DB query inside loop, missing index, missing parameter validation. |\n| **P3** | **Low (Nit / Suggestion)** | Minor formatting, naming improvements, leftover comments/TODOs, minor doc polish. | Variable naming clarity, typos in docstrings, cleaning leftover TODO comments. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Comprehensive Review Checklist\n\n### A. Logic & Correctness\n- [ ] **Edge Cases**: Does the code handle null/nil/undefined, empty collections, zero values, boundary numbers, and unexpected inputs?\n- [ ] **State & Concurrency**: Are shared state mutations thread-safe? Are locks acquired/released properly without deadlock risks?\n- [ ] **Control Flow**: Are all conditional branches covered? Do loops have guaranteed termination conditions?\n- [ ] **Error Propagation**: Are errors caught and logged/surfaced appropriately, rather than swallowed silently (`catch (Exception e) {}`)?\n\n### B. Security & Credentials\n- [ ] **No Hardcoded Secrets**: Are API keys, passwords, bearer tokens, or private keys excluded from code and config?\n- [ ] **Input Validation & Sanitization**: Are external inputs validated before processing or passing to system shells, DB queries, or HTML rendering?\n- [ ] **Authentication & Authorization**: Do endpoints verify user identity and check permissions before executing state changes?\n- [ ] **Safe Dependencies**: Are newly added packages pinned to trusted versions without known vulnerabilities?\n\n### C. Architecture & API Design\n- [ ] **Preserve API Contracts**: Are public method signatures, REST endpoints, and schema definitions backward compatible?\n- [ ] **Single Responsibility**: Are modules, classes, and functions focused on a clear, single responsibility?\n- [ ] **Coupling & Cohesion**: Is the new code properly modularized without introducing circular dependencies or leaky abstractions?\n- [ ] **Idempotence**: Are retry loops or state-changing operations safe to re-execute on transient failures?\n\n### D. Performance & Resource Efficiency\n- [ ] **N+1 Queries**: Are database or remote API calls executed in batches rather than inside loops?\n- [ ] **Resource Cleanup**: Are file handles, database connections, streams, and web sockets closed explicitly (or managed via try-with-resources / context managers)?\n- [ ] **Memory & Allocation**: Are large datasets streamed or paginated rather than loaded fully into memory at once?\n\n### E. Test Coverage & Quality\n- [ ] **Test Coverage**: Do new features or bug fixes include corresponding unit or integration tests?\n- [ ] **Test Quality**: Do tests verify actual assertions rather than just checking that code runs without throwing?\n- [ ] **Edge Case Tests**: Are failure modes, invalid inputs, and error handlers covered by unit tests?\n\n---\n\n## 3. Review Feedback Guidelines\n\n1. **Be Specific**: Always reference the exact file line number, function name, and context.\n2. **Explain the \"Why\"**: Don't just say \"change this\". Explain the risk or benefit (e.g., \"This could lead to a race condition if two threads call `transact!` simultaneously...\").\n3. **Provide Concrete Fixes**: Offer concrete, copy-pasteable diff snippets where appropriate.\n4. **Acknowledge Good Work**: Highlight well-crafted solutions, thorough tests, or clean refactorings.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nPR Reviewer Utility Script for Git-based Code Reviews.\nParses git diffs, analyzes churn and file risk categories, scans for security smells\nand debugging code, and produces structured markdown or JSON review reports.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass, field\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Finding:\n    severity: str  # P0 (Critical), P1 (High), P2 (Medium), P3 (Low)\n    category: str  # Security, Debug, Quality, ErrorHandling, TestCoverage\n    file_path: str\n    line_number: Optional[int]\n    message: str\n    snippet: str\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass FileStat:\n    path: str\n    additions: int\n    deletions: int\n    category: str\n    risk_level: str  # High, Medium, Low\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass ReviewSummary:\n    target: str\n    total_files: int\n    total_additions: int\n    total_deletions: int\n    test_additions: int\n    source_additions: int\n    test_to_source_ratio: float\n    file_stats: List[FileStat] = field(default_factory=list)\n    findings: List[Finding] = field(default_factory=list)\n    commits: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n\n\ndef run_git_command(args: List[str], cwd: Optional[str] = None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Helper to run git commands cleanly.\"\"\"\n    cmd = [\"git\"] + args\n    try:\n        res = subprocess.run(\n            cmd,\n            cwd=cwd,\n            stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n            stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\n            text=True,\n            check=True,\n        )\n        return res.stdout.strip()\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n        sys.stderr.write(f\"Git command failed: {' '.join(cmd)}\\nError: {e.stderr}\\n\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Git execution failed: {e.stderr.strip()}\")\n\n\ndef categorize_file(file_path: str) -> Tuple[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"Categorizes file type and assigns risk level.\"\"\"\n    path_lower = file_path.lower()\n\n    # Security & Auth\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\"auth\", \"secret\", \"crypto\", \"token\", \"permission\", \"jwt\", \"oauth\", \"password\"]):\n        return \"Security/Auth\", \"High\"\n\n    # Database & Schema\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\"migration\", \"schema\", \".sql\", \"entity\", \"db/\"]):\n        return \"Database/Schema\", \"High\"\n\n    # Infrastructure & Config\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\"docker\", \"terraform\", \".tf\", \".env\", \"k8s\", \"helm\", \"ci/cd\", \".github/workflows\"]):\n        return \"Infra/Config\", \"High\"\n    if any(file_path.endswith(ext) for ext in [\"package.json\", \"deps.edn\", \"Cargo.toml\", \"go.mod\", \"requirements.txt\", \"pom.xml\", \"build.gradle\"]):\n        return \"Dependencies\", \"Medium\"\n\n    # API / Interfaces\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\"proto\", \"openapi\", \"swagger\", \"graphql\", \"router\", \"controller\", \"api/\"]):\n        return \"API/Contract\", \"Medium\"\n\n    # Tests\n    if any(k in path_lower for k in [\"test\", \"spec\", \"mock\", \"fixture\", \"e2e\"]):\n        return \"Tests\", \"Low\"\n\n    # Documentation\n    if any(file_path.endswith(ext) for ext in [\".md\", \".rst\", \".txt\", \"LICENSE\"]):\n        return \"Documentation\", \"Low\"\n\n    # Core source\n    return \"Source Code\", \"Medium\"\n\n\ndef scan_diff_content(diff_text: str) -> List[Finding]:\n    \"\"\"Scans diff text for added code smells and risks.\"\"\"\n    findings: List[Finding] = []\n\n    # Patterns to match added lines\n    patterns = [\n        # Secret leaks\n        (\n            r\"(?i)^\\+.*(api[_\\-]?key|secret[_\\-]?key|bearer\\s+[a-z0-9_\\-\\.]{20,}|private[_\\-]?key)\\s*[:=]\\s*['\\\"][A-Za-z0-9%+\\/=\\-_]{8,}['\\\"]\",\n            \"P0\",\n            \"Security\",\n            \"Possible hardcoded credential or secret detected.\",\n        ),\n        (\n            r\"^\\+.*-----BEGIN (RSA|OPENSSH|EC|PRIVATE) KEY-----\",\n            \"P0\",\n            \"Security\",\n            \"Embedded private key detected.\",\n        ),\n        # Debug code left behind\n        (\n            r\"^\\+.*\\b(console\\.log|print\\(|debugger;|binding\\.pry|import pdb; pdb\\.set_trace|println!|fmt\\.Println)\\b\",\n            \"P3\",\n            \"Debug\",\n            \"Leftover debug statement detected.\",\n        ),\n        # Dangerous functions\n        (\n            r\"^\\+.*\\b(eval\\(|exec\\(|os\\.system\\(|subprocess\\.Popen\\(.*shell\\s*=\\s*True|dangerouslySetInnerHTML)\\b\",\n            \"P1\",\n            \"Security\",\n            \"Potentially unsafe dynamic execution or shell invocation.\",\n        ),\n        # Swallowed exceptions\n        (\n            r\"^\\+.*\\b(catch\\s*\\([^\\)]*\\)\\s*\\{\\s*\\}|except:\\s*pass|rescue\\s*=>\\s*nil)\\b\",\n            \"P2\",\n            \"ErrorHandling\",\n            \"Swallowed exception without logging or handling.\",\n        ),\n        # Potential SQL Injection\n        (\n            r\"(?i)^\\+.*((select|insert|update|delete)\\s+.*%s|(select|insert|update|delete)\\s+.*\\$[a-z0-9_]+|(select|insert|update|delete)\\s+.*\\+\\s*[a-z0-9_]+)\",\n            \"P1\",\n            \"Security\",\n            \"Potential SQL string concatenation detected. Use parameterized queries.\",\n        ),\n        # TODO / FIXME additions\n        (\n            r\"(?i)^\\+.*\\b(TODO|FIXME|HACK|XXX)\\b\",\n            \"P3\",\n            \"Quality\",\n            \"Added TODO/FIXME annotation. Verify if it should be resolved before merging.\",\n        ),\n        # Hardcoded Localhost / IPs\n        (\n            r\"^\\+.*(http://localhost|http://127\\.0\\.0\\.1|127\\.0\\.0\\.1:[0-9]+)\",\n            \"P2\",\n            \"Config\",\n            \"Hardcoded localhost or loopback address found in diff.\",\n        ),\n    ]\n\n    current_file = \"\"\n    line_num = 0\n\n    for line in diff_text.splitlines():\n        if line.startswith(\"--- a/\"):\n            continue\n        if line.startswith(\"+++ b/\"):\n            current_file = line[6:]\n            continue\n        if line.startswith(\"@@ \"):\n            # Extract starting line number for b/ side\n            match = re.search(r\"\\+([0-9]+)\", line)\n            if match:\n                line_num = int(match.group(1)) - 1\n            continue\n\n        if line.startswith(\"+\") and not line.startswith(\"+++\"):\n            line_num += 1\n            for regex, severity, category, message in patterns:\n                if re.search(regex, line):\n                    findings.append(\n                        Finding(\n                            severity=severity,\n                            category=category,\n                            file_path=current_file,\n                            line_number=line_num,\n                            message=message,\n                            snippet=line[1:].strip(),\n                        )\n                    )\n        elif not line.startswith(\"-\"):\n            line_num += 1\n\n    return findings\n\n\ndef analyze_git_target(target: str, repo_dir: Optional[str] = None) -> ReviewSummary:\n    \"\"\"Analyzes git target (e.g. main...HEAD, HEAD~1, staged, working).\"\"\"\n    git_args = []\n    log_args = []\n\n    if target == \"staged\":\n        git_args = [\"diff\", \"--cached\"]\n        log_args = [\"log\", \"-n\", \"5\", \"--oneline\"]\n    elif target == \"working\":\n        git_args = [\"diff\", \"HEAD\"]\n        log_args = [\"log\", \"-n\", \"5\", \"--oneline\"]\n    else:\n        git_args = [\"diff\", target]\n        if \"...\" in target:\n            base, head = target.split(\"...\")\n            log_args = [\"log\", \"--oneline\", f\"{base}..{head}\"]\n        elif \"..\" in target:\n            log_args = [\"log\", \"--oneline\", target]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
