{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat AGENTS.md && nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '590,980p'\"","aggregated_output":"# ==============================================================================\n# datom.world – Development Rules & Architectural Foundations\n# ==============================================================================\n\nSee [`docs/design/datom.world.md`](./docs/design/datom.world.md) for master architecture, core philosophy, foundational axioms, non-negotiable invariants, code style, development workflow, and operational guides (testing, team roles, agent delegation, website formats).\n   590\t              (cond (nil? prior) (assoc index (first row) row)\n   591\t                    (same-value? prior row) index\n   592\t                    :else (throw-prelude \"Packet address conflict\"\n   593\t                                         {:address (first row)}))))\n   594\t          {}\n   595\t          (mapcat second packets)))\n   596\t\n   597\t\n   598\t(def ^:private pending-expansion-origin\n   599\t  \"The construction origin the prelude attaches to every node the\n   600\t   macro's code builds during one invocation (ruling U1: identity comes\n   601\t   from the construction event, never from comparing content\n   602\t   addresses). `expand-call` substitutes the recorded expansion event's\n   603\t   `[:expansion record-address]` origin for it when the output's\n   604\t   occurrence correspondence is read — the placeholder never reaches a\n   605\t   table, a row, or an event it does not belong to.\"\n   606\t  [:expansion ::pending])\n   607\t\n   608\t\n   609\t(defn- with-origin-of\n   610\t  \"Tag packet `p` with `f`, its construction origin function: `(f rel)`\n   611\t   answers the origin of the occurrence at `rel`, a path relative to\n   612\t   `p`'s root — the pending expansion origin for a node the macro's\n   613\t   code constructed, or, below a child coordinate that retains a\n   614\t   passed-through packet, that packet's own origin function. The\n   615\t   function rides the packet's metadata, so it is content-addressing\n   616\t   invisible and never leaks into a final tree.\"\n   617\t  [p f]\n   618\t  (vary-meta p assoc ::origin-of f))\n   619\t\n   620\t\n   621\t(defn- origin-of-fn\n   622\t  \"The construction origin function packet `p` carries, or nil.\"\n   623\t  [p]\n   624\t  (::origin-of (meta p)))\n   625\t\n   626\t\n   627\t(def ^:private tracking-meta-keys\n   628\t  \"The private provenance entries the expander rides on packet values.\n   629\t   They are host functions, so they must never enter a hashed or\n   630\t   validated data slot (P1-2); every other metadata entry is the\n   631\t   caller's legitimate data and is preserved.\"\n   632\t  #{::origin-of})\n   633\t\n   634\t\n   635\t(defn- strip-tracking\n   636\t  \"Remove only the private tracking entries, recursively, from `x`:\n   637\t   every collection element, map key and value, and every metadata map\n   638\t   (including metadata on metadata) is visited, so a packet nested at\n   639\t   any depth inside a literal payload loses its host-function origin\n   640\t   while legitimate user metadata survives untouched.\"\n   641\t  [x]\n   642\t  (let [x' (cond (record? x) x\n   643\t                 (map? x) (into (empty x)\n   644\t                                (map (fn [[k v]]\n   645\t                                       [(strip-tracking k)\n   646\t                                        (strip-tracking v)]))\n   647\t                                x)\n   648\t                 (set? x) (into (empty x) (map strip-tracking) x)\n   649\t                 (vector? x) (mapv strip-tracking x)\n   650\t                 (sequential? x) (with-meta\n   651\t                                   (apply list (map strip-tracking x))\n   652\t                                   nil)\n   653\t                 :else x)\n   654\t        m (meta x)]\n   655\t    (if m\n   656\t      (let [m' (strip-tracking\n   657\t                 (apply dissoc m tracking-meta-keys))]\n   658\t        (with-meta x' (when-not (and (empty? m') (nil? (meta m'))) m')))\n   659\t      x')))\n   660\t\n   661\t\n   662\t(defn- packet-has-application?\n   663\t  \"True when packet `p` contains an `:application` occurrence, the only\n   664\t   occurrences whose provenance a correspondence ever reads.\"\n   665\t  [p]\n   666\t  (boolean (and (packet? p)\n   667\t                (some #(= :application (row-tag %)) (second p)))))\n   668\t\n   669\t\n   670\t(defn- register-lineage!\n   671\t  \"Record packet `p` in the invocation `lineage` (an atom of entries)\n   672\t   under the identity of its rows vector. Host decomposition\n   673\t   (`first`/`rest`/`get`) hands that very object to reassembly, so the\n   674\t   entry is how a rebuilt packet proves it is this packet retained,\n   675\t   never a content twin built anew. Returns `p`.\"\n   676\t  [lineage p]\n   677\t  (when (and lineage (packet? p) (origin-of-fn p))\n   678\t    (when-not (some #(identical? (second p) (:rows %)) @lineage)\n   679\t      (swap! lineage conj {:root (first p), :rows (second p),\n   680\t                           :fn (origin-of-fn p)})))\n   681\t  p)\n   682\t\n   683\t\n   684\t(defn- lineage-origin-for\n   685\t  \"The retained origin function for candidate packet `c`, or nil when\n   686\t   no registered packet unambiguously accounts for it. Content\n   687\t   equality alone never suffices — a freshly built twin holds equal\n   688\t   but distinct row objects and recovers nothing here (ruling U1).\n   689\t\n   690\t   Exact container lineage is preferred: a registered packet whose\n   691\t   rows vector is the very object `c` carries (host decomposition\n   692\t   hands that object to reassembly) is occurrence-specific, so it\n   693\t   wins over any row-level match. Row-level recovery — the root\n   694\t   matches and every row is `identical?` to a registered packet's\n   695\t   row in order — is taken only when exactly one distinct origin\n   696\t   function matches: distinct occurrences of identical content share\n   697\t   row objects (`packet-of` retrieves them from one index), so a\n   698\t   first-match pick among ambiguous row-level candidates would\n   699\t   attach another occurrence's origin. Ambiguity is refused (nil),\n   700\t   which downstream reads as missing provenance, never as a guess.\"\n   701\t  [lineage c]\n   702\t  (when (and lineage (packet? c) (nil? (origin-of-fn c)))\n   703\t    (let [entries (filter #(= (:root %) (first c)) @lineage)\n   704\t          rows (second c)\n   705\t          only-fn (fn [es]\n   706\t                    (let [fns (distinct (map :fn es))]\n   707\t                      (when (= 1 (count fns)) (first fns))))\n   708\t          exact (filter #(identical? (:rows %) rows) entries)]\n   709\t      (if (seq exact)\n   710\t        (only-fn exact)\n   711\t        (only-fn (filter #(and (= (count (:rows %)) (count rows))\n   712\t                               (every? true?\n   713\t                                       (map identical? (:rows %) rows)))\n   714\t                         entries))))))\n   715\t\n   716\t\n   717\t(def ^:private missing-provenance-origin\n   718\t  \"The origin an unaccounted child answers below its coordinate: no\n   719\t   sanctioned operation threaded provenance to it, so nothing may\n   720\t   relabel its occurrences as this expansion's construction (P1-1).\n   721\t   `output-correspondence` carries the marker through and\n   722\t   `expand-call` refuses the output as `:missing-provenance`; the\n   723\t   marker never reaches a table, a row, or an event.\"\n   724\t  [:expansion ::missing])\n   725\t\n   726\t\n   727\t(defn- constructed-origin-fn\n   728\t  \"The origin function of a packet the prelude constructed: its root\n   729\t   occurrence carries the pending expansion origin; a relative path\n   730\t   below a child coordinate delegates to the packet passed for that\n   731\t   child — a spliced operand retains its own incoming origin, however\n   732\t   the macro's code embedded it. `recover` answers a child packet's\n   733\t   retained origin function when the packet itself carries none (it\n   734\t   was rebuilt by decomposition/reassembly); a child neither source\n   735\t   accounts for answers `missing-provenance-origin` below its\n   736\t   coordinate, which the expander refuses rather than reads as\n   737\t   construction.\"\n   738\t  ([coord-children] (constructed-origin-fn coord-children (fn [_] nil)))\n   739\t  ([coord-children recover]\n   740\t   (fn [rel]\n   741\t     (if (empty? rel)\n   742\t       pending-expansion-origin\n   743\t       (if-some [child (get coord-children (first rel))]\n   744\t         (if-some [f (or (origin-of-fn child) (recover child))]\n   745\t           (f (subvec rel 1))\n   746\t           missing-provenance-origin)\n   747\t         pending-expansion-origin)))))\n   748\t\n   749\t\n   750\t(defn- construct\n   751\t  \"Intern `body` over the rows of its child `packets`; a closed packet.\n   752\t   Every node interned here is CONSTRUCTED by the expansion's code\n   753\t   (ruling U1), so the result packet carries the construction origin\n   754\t   function and the output's per-occurrence origins are read from this\n   755\t   construction history — never inferred by comparing content\n   756\t   addresses: a constructed node whose content equals a retained\n   757\t   node's stays distinct, because its origin answers through this\n   758\t   function and not through its address.\n   759\t\n   760\t   Values entering `:data`/`:key` slots are stripped of private\n   761\t   tracking metadata first (P1-2), before hashing and validation.\n   762\t   Missing child provenance never proves construction (P1-1): the\n   763\t   result's origin function answers the missing marker below an\n   764\t   unaccounted child and the expander refuses such an output.\"\n   765\t  ([body packets] (construct body packets nil))\n   766\t  ([body packets lineage]\n   767\t   (let [recover (fn [child] (lineage-origin-for lineage child))]\n   768\t     (let [tag (first body)\n   769\t           slots (get working-grammar tag)\n   770\t           body (if (and slots (= (count slots) (count (rest body))))\n   771\t                  (into [tag]\n   772\t                        (map (fn [[_ kind] v]\n   773\t                               (if (contains? #{:data :key} kind)\n   774\t                                 (strip-tracking v)\n   775\t                                 v))\n   776\t                             slots\n   777\t                             (rest body)))\n   778\t                  body)\n   779\t           index (merge-packets packets)\n   780\t           [index a] (intern-body index body)\n   781\t           coord-children (into {}\n   782\t                                (map (fn [[place p]] [(first place) p]))\n   783\t                                (map vector (child-places (get index a)) packets))]\n   784\t       (with-origin-of (packet-of index a)\n   785\t         (constructed-origin-fn coord-children recover))))))\n   786\t\n   787\t\n   788\t(defn- root-row\n   789\t  [[root rows]]\n   790\t  (some #(when (= root (first %)) %) rows))\n   791\t\n   792\t\n   793\t(defn- literal-packet\n   794\t  ([v] (literal-packet v nil))\n   795\t  ([v lineage] (construct [:literal (strip-tracking v)] [] lineage)))\n   796\t\n   797\t\n   798\t(defn- application-packet\n   799\t  ([operator operands] (application-packet operator operands nil))\n   800\t  ([operator operands lineage]\n   801\t   (construct [:application (first operator) (mapv first operands) false]\n   802\t              (cons operator operands)\n   803\t              lineage)))\n   804\t\n   805\t\n   806\t(defn- lambda-packet\n   807\t  ([params body] (lambda-packet params body nil))\n   808\t  ([params body lineage]\n   809\t   (when-not (and (sequential? params) (every? symbol? params))\n   810\t     (throw-prelude \"yin/lambda params must be symbols\" {:op 'yin/lambda}))\n   811\t   (construct [:lambda (vec params) (first body)] [body] lineage)))\n   812\t\n   813\t\n   814\t(defn- name-of\n   815\t  [tree]\n   816\t  (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/name-of tree))\n   817\t        v (nth row 2 nil)]\n   818\t    (cond (= :variable (row-tag row)) v\n   819\t          (and (= :literal (row-tag row)) (symbol? v)) v\n   820\t          (and (= :literal (row-tag row)) (string? v)) (symbol v)\n   821\t          :else (throw-prelude \"yin/name-of reads a variable, literal symbol, or literal string\"\n   822\t                               {:op 'yin/name-of}))))\n   823\t\n   824\t\n   825\t(defn- sequence-body\n   826\t  \"The reference `do` lowering: `(do a b c)` is `((fn [_] ((fn [_] c) b)) a)`;\n   827\t   one form is itself and none is the literal nil.\"\n   828\t  ([trees] (sequence-body trees nil))\n   829\t  ([trees lineage]\n   830\t   (let [trees (vec trees)]\n   831\t     (doseq [t trees] (need-packet 'yin/sequence-body t))\n   832\t     (case (count trees)\n   833\t       0 (literal-packet nil lineage)\n   834\t       1 (first trees)\n   835\t       (application-packet\n   836\t         (lambda-packet ['_]\n   837\t                        (sequence-body (subvec trees 1) lineage)\n   838\t                        lineage)\n   839\t         [(first trees)]\n   840\t         lineage)))))\n   841\t\n   842\t\n   843\t(defn- slot-of\n   844\t  ([tree n] (slot-of tree n nil))\n   845\t  ([tree n lineage]\n   846\t   (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/slot tree))\n   847\t        kinds (into {} (slot-kinds (row-tag row)))\n   848\t        index (packet-index tree)\n   849\t        ;; an extracted slot is input syntax READ, not built: the\n   850\t        ;; extracted packet retains the source packet's construction\n   851\t        ;; origin function, descending through the slot's coordinate.\n   852\t        ;; A source no operation accounted for answers the missing\n   853\t        ;; marker, never fabricated construction (P1-1).\n   854\t        ofn (or (origin-of-fn tree)\n   855\t                (lineage-origin-for lineage tree)\n   856\t                (fn [_] missing-provenance-origin))]\n   857\t    (when-not (and (integer? n) (contains? kinds n))\n   858\t      (throw-prelude \"yin/slot position names no grammar slot\"\n   859\t                     {:op 'yin/slot, :position n}))\n   860\t    (case (get kinds n)\n   861\t      :node (with-origin-of (packet-of index (nth row n))\n   862\t              (fn [rel] (ofn (into [n] rel))))\n   863\t      :nodes (map-indexed (fn [i c]\n   864\t                            (with-origin-of (packet-of index c)\n   865\t                              (fn [rel] (ofn (into [[n i]] rel)))))\n   866\t                          (nth row n))\n   867\t      (nth row n)))))\n   868\t\n   869\t\n   870\t(defn prelude\n   871\t  \"The closed body environment (§5.3): the pure standard primitives (no\n   872\t   `require`, no stream or FFI constructor) and the row-native constructors,\n   873\t   each consuming and returning self-contained tree packets. `gensym` is the\n   874\t   invocation-local `yin/gensym-sym`.\n   875\t\n   876\t   The collection primitives are provenance-aware within one invocation\n   877\t   (P1-1): decomposing a packet (`first`/`rest`/`get`) registers its\n   878\t   lineage, and reassembling one (`conj`/`assoc`/`vec`) reattaches the\n   879\t   retained origin function when the rebuilt packet holds the very row\n   880\t   objects it was decomposed from. A packet rebuilt any other way\n   881\t   carries no provenance and is refused downstream rather than\n   882\t   relabelled as construction.\"\n   883\t  ([gensym] (prelude gensym (atom [])))\n   884\t  ([gensym lineage]\n   885\t   (let [recover-packet (fn [result]\n   886\t                          (cond (not (packet? result)) result\n   887\t                                (origin-of-fn result)\n   888\t                                (register-lineage! lineage result)\n   889\t                                :else (if-some [f (lineage-origin-for\n   890\t                                                    lineage result)]\n   891\t                                        (with-origin-of result f)\n   892\t                                        result)))\n   893\t         wrap (fn [sym f]\n   894\t                (let [entry (get vm/primitives sym)]\n   895\t                  (if (and (map? entry)\n   896\t                           (contains? entry :yin.k/function))\n   897\t                    (assoc entry :yin.k/function f)\n   898\t                    f)))\n   899\t         p-first (fn [coll]\n   900\t                   (register-lineage! lineage coll)\n   901\t                   (recover-packet (first coll)))\n   902\t         p-rest (fn [coll]\n   903\t                  (register-lineage! lineage coll)\n   904\t                  (vec (rest coll)))\n   905\t         p-conj (fn [coll & xs]\n   906\t                  (register-lineage! lineage coll)\n   907\t                  (doseq [x xs] (register-lineage! lineage x))\n   908\t                  (recover-packet (apply conj coll xs)))\n   909\t         p-assoc (fn [m & kvs]\n   910\t                   (register-lineage! lineage m)\n   911\t                   (recover-packet (apply assoc m kvs)))\n   912\t         p-get (fn\n   913\t                 ([m k]\n   914\t                  (register-lineage! lineage m)\n   915\t                  (recover-packet (get m k)))\n   916\t                 ([m k not-found]\n   917\t                  (register-lineage! lineage m)\n   918\t                  (recover-packet (get m k not-found))))\n   919\t         p-vec (fn [coll]\n   920\t                 (recover-packet (vec coll)))]\n   921\t     (merge\n   922\t       (dissoc vm/primitives 'require 'try-require 'bytes->str)\n   923\t       {'first (wrap 'first p-first),\n   924\t        'rest (wrap 'rest p-rest),\n   925\t        'conj (wrap 'conj p-conj),\n   926\t        'assoc (wrap 'assoc p-assoc),\n   927\t        'get (wrap 'get p-get),\n   928\t        'vec (wrap 'vec p-vec),\n   929\t        'yin/tag (fn [tree] (row-tag (root-row (need-packet 'yin/tag tree)))),\n   930\t        'yin/slot (fn [tree n] (slot-of tree n lineage)),\n   931\t        'yin/literal (fn [v] (literal-packet v lineage)),\n   932\t        'yin/variable (fn [sym]\n   933\t                        (when-not (symbol? sym)\n   934\t                          (throw-prelude \"yin/variable expects a symbol\" {:op 'yin/variable}))\n   935\t                        (construct [:variable sym] [] lineage)),\n   936\t        'yin/lambda (fn [params body]\n   937\t                      (lambda-packet params (need-packet 'yin/lambda body)\n   938\t                                     lineage)),\n   939\t        'yin/application (fn [operator operands]\n   940\t                           (need-packet 'yin/application operator)\n   941\t                           (doseq [o operands] (need-packet 'yin/application o))\n   942\t                           (application-packet operator (vec operands)\n   943\t                                               lineage)),\n   944\t        'yin/if (fn [t c a]\n   945\t                  (doseq [x [t c a]] (need-packet 'yin/if x))\n   946\t                  (construct [:if (first t) (first c) (first a)] [t c a]\n   947\t                             lineage)),\n   948\t        'yin/sequence-body (fn [trees] (sequence-body trees lineage)),\n   949\t        'yin/make-lambda (fn [params-tree body]\n   950\t                           (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/make-lambda params-tree))]\n   951\t                             (when-not (and (= :literal (row-tag row))\n   952\t                                            (vector? (nth row 2))\n   953\t                                            (every? symbol? (nth row 2)))\n   954\t                               (throw-prelude \"yin/make-lambda reads a literal parameter vector\"\n   955\t                                              {:op 'yin/make-lambda}))\n   956\t                             (lambda-packet (nth row 2)\n   957\t                                            (need-packet 'yin/make-lambda body)\n   958\t                                            lineage))),\n   959\t        'yin/make-def (fn [name-tree value-tree]\n   960\t                        (application-packet\n   961\t                          (construct [:variable 'yin/def] [] lineage)\n   962\t                          [(literal-packet (name-of name-tree) lineage)\n   963\t                           (need-packet 'yin/make-def value-tree)]\n   964\t                          lineage)),\n   965\t        'yin/name-of name-of,\n   966\t        'yin/gensym-sym gensym}))))\n   967\t\n   968\t\n   969\t(def ^:private suspending-tags\n   970\t  #{:vm/park :vm/resume :dao.stream.apply/call})\n   971\t\n   972\t\n   973\t(def ^:private effect-tags\n   974\t  #{:stream/make :stream/put :stream/cursor :stream/next :stream/close})\n   975\t\n   976\t\n   977\t(defn- catch-message\n   978\t  [e]\n   979\t  (or (ex-message e) (str e)))\n   980\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '1,170p;1040,1130p;1310,1490p' && rg -n 'lineage|origin-of|missing-provenance|pending-expansion|rebuild|repack|U1' test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '1,170p;1040,1130p;1310,1490p' && rg -n 'lineage|origin-of|missing-provenance|pending-expansion|rebuild|repack|U1' test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.macro\n     2\t  \"The row-native macro expander (`docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md`, Phase 1).\n     3\t\n     4\t   A process between two media: it observes `program-in` batches\n     5\t   `[:yin.program/batch trees run-index declaration-rows harvest-rows\n     6\t   call-site-claims]` — the trailing element present only when some\n     7\t   member's frontend claimed call-site (C1) coverage, holding one\n     8\t   boolean verdict per member, so every older five-element batch is\n     9\t   still a valid unclaimed batch —\n    10\t   rewrites the selected tree to a fixpoint, and appends one canonical tree\n    11\t   packet `[root rows]` to `program-out`, with one event row per attempt on\n    12\t   an optional log medium. Evaluators know nothing of any of this (decision\n    13\t   1): a macro call is an ordinary `:application` row, macro-ness is an\n    14\t   occurrence declaration beside the tree, and definitions leave as ordinary\n    15\t   syntax or as a literal naming the lowered macro.\n    16\t\n    17\t   Everything here is a value threaded through the step: the macro store,\n    18\t   attempt counter, batch coordinate, and incarnation token live in `ctx`\n    19\t   (§3.1). Expansion failure is data (decision 12); a throw is a defect or a\n    20\t   terminal stream outcome.\"\n    21\t  (:refer-clojure :exclude [flush load])\n    22\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n    23\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    24\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n    25\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    26\t            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n    27\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]))\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t;; =============================================================================\n    31\t;; Grammar, rows, and packets (§1)\n    32\t;; =============================================================================\n    33\t\n    34\t(def ^:private standin-tag :yin.macro/defined)\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\t(def ^:private working-grammar\n    38\t  \"The canonical §2.3 table plus the one working row the expander interns\n    39\t   and lowers itself: `[S :yin.macro/defined name k]` (§3.2 step 3). It is\n    40\t   admitted only in operand and result packets, never in input or output.\"\n    41\t  (assoc vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar standin-tag [[:name :sym] [:k :int]]))\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(defn- grammar\n    45\t  [working?]\n    46\t  (if working? working-grammar vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn- row-tag\n    50\t  [row]\n    51\t  (nth row 1))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn- intern-row\n    55\t  \"The full row for `body`: its content address prepended (§1.1).\"\n    56\t  [body]\n    57\t  (into [(jing/segment-key body)] body))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(defn- slot-kinds\n    61\t  \"`[[position kind] ...]` for a tag's grammar slots, positions being full-row\n    62\t   positions (address 0, tag 1, first slot 2).\"\n    63\t  [tag]\n    64\t  (map-indexed (fn [i [_ kind]] [(+ i 2) kind]) (get working-grammar tag)))\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(defn- child-places\n    68\t  \"`[[coordinate child-address] ...]` of one row in grammar order: a `node`\n    69\t   slot's coordinate is its full-row position, a `nodes` child's is\n    70\t   `[position i]` (§2.1).\"\n    71\t  [row]\n    72\t  (mapcat (fn [[pos kind]]\n    73\t            (case kind\n    74\t              :node [[pos (nth row pos)]]\n    75\t              :nodes (map-indexed (fn [i c] [[pos i] c]) (nth row pos))\n    76\t              nil))\n    77\t          (slot-kinds (row-tag row))))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(defn- with-child\n    81\t  \"`row`'s body with the child at coordinate `coord` replaced by `address`.\"\n    82\t  [row coord address]\n    83\t  (let [body (subvec row 1)]\n    84\t    (if (vector? coord)\n    85\t      (let [[pos i] coord]\n    86\t        (assoc body (dec pos) (assoc (nth row pos) i address)))\n    87\t      (assoc body (dec coord) address))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn- reachable\n    91\t  \"Addresses reachable from `root` through `index`, first-encounter preorder\n    92\t   in grammar order. Assumes the index is closed and acyclic.\"\n    93\t  [index root]\n    94\t  (loop [stack (list root)\n    95\t         seen #{}\n    96\t         order []]\n    97\t    (if-let [a (first stack)]\n    98\t      (if (contains? seen a)\n    99\t        (recur (rest stack) seen order)\n   100\t        (recur (reduce conj (rest stack) (reverse (map second (child-places (get index a)))))\n   101\t               (conj seen a)\n   102\t               (conj order a)))\n   103\t      order)))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(defn- packet-of\n   107\t  \"The self-contained tree packet `[root rows]` rooted at `root` (§1.2). Row\n   108\t   order is preorder, which is deterministic but carries no meaning.\"\n   109\t  [index root]\n   110\t  [root (mapv #(get index %) (reachable index root))])\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(defn tree-packet\n   114\t  \"Convert a projected row set `{:root id :rows {id row}}` (the shape\n   115\t   `yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode` returns) to a tree packet `[root rows]`.\"\n   116\t  [{:keys [root rows]}]\n   117\t  (packet-of rows root))\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(defn packet->row-set\n   121\t  \"Convert a canonical tree packet to `{:root id :rows {id row}}`, the shape\n   122\t   the evaluator loaders take.\"\n   123\t  [[root rows]]\n   124\t  {:root root, :rows (into {} (map (fn [r] [(first r) r])) rows)})\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn ast->packet\n   128\t  \"Project a map AST to its canonical tree packet.\"\n   129\t  [ast]\n   130\t  (tree-packet (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))\n   131\t\n   132\t\n   133\t(defn- same-value?\n   134\t  \"`=` that also compares metadata at every depth: the transitional address\n   135\t   encoder does not hash scalar metadata, so two bodies may share an address\n   136\t   while differing there, which is an address conflict (§5.3, §7.2).\"\n   137\t  [a b]\n   138\t  (and (= a b)\n   139\t       (= (meta a) (meta b))\n   140\t       (or (nil? (meta a)) (same-value? (meta a) (meta b)))\n   141\t       (cond (map? a) (every? (fn [[k v]]\n   142\t                                (let [[k' v'] (find b k)]\n   143\t                                  (and (same-value? k k') (same-value? v v'))))\n   144\t                              a)\n   145\t             (set? a) (every? (fn [e] (same-value? e (some #(when (= e %) %) b))) a)\n   146\t             (sequential? a) (every? true? (map same-value? a b))\n   147\t             :else true)))\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\t;; =============================================================================\n   151\t;; Packet validation (§7.1, §7.2)\n   152\t;; =============================================================================\n   153\t\n   154\t(defn- standin-shaped?\n   155\t  \"A vector that reads as a working stand-in row or body.\"\n   156\t  [x]\n   157\t  (and (vector? x)\n   158\t       (or (= standin-tag (first x))\n   159\t           (and (< 1 (count x)) (= standin-tag (nth x 1))))))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn- marker-in?\n   163\t  \"True when a stand-in-shaped vector appears anywhere inside a value.\"\n   164\t  [x]\n   165\t  (or (standin-shaped? x)\n   166\t      (and (map? x) (some (fn [[k v]] (or (marker-in? k) (marker-in? v))) x))\n   167\t      (and (coll? x) (not (map? x)) (some marker-in? x))\n   168\t      (and (some? (meta x)) (marker-in? (meta x)))))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n  1040\t      (if (< m n)\n  1041\t        {:expected n, :got m}\n  1042\t        {:env (assoc (zipmap fixed args) rest-sym (vec (drop n args)))})\n  1043\t      (if (not= m n)\n  1044\t        {:expected n, :got m}\n  1045\t        {:env (zipmap fixed args)}))))\n  1046\t\n  1047\t\n  1048\t(defn- attempt-id\n  1049\t  [ctx counter]\n  1050\t  [(get-in ctx [:incarnation :yin.expander/token]) counter])\n  1051\t\n  1052\t\n  1053\t(defn macro-entry\n  1054\t  \"A macro-store value: a self-contained lambda tree `packet` with the AST\n  1055\t   `contract` it was produced under. The store holds only these. The\n  1056\t   transformer runner verifies the contract before it executes the packet\n  1057\t   (Rule R: a persistent or supplied code packet is never relabelled), and\n  1058\t   the expander stamps only what it harvests itself, under\n  1059\t   `vm/ast-contract`.\"\n  1060\t  [packet contract]\n  1061\t  {:yin.macro/tree packet, :yin.macro/contract contract})\n  1062\t\n  1063\t\n  1064\t(defn- verified-tree\n  1065\t  \"The packet of a macro-store value after its contract is verified\n  1066\t   against `vm/ast-contract`: `:contract-missing` for a bare packet or an\n  1067\t   entry without one, `:contract-mismatch` for an old stamp.\"\n  1068\t  [entry]\n  1069\t  (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract\n  1070\t                      (when (map? entry) (:yin.macro/contract entry)))\n  1071\t  (:yin.macro/tree entry))\n  1072\t\n  1073\t\n  1074\t(defn- check-store!\n  1075\t  \"A supplied macro store: no reserved name is a macro (Rule R), and every\n  1076\t   entry carries the current AST contract. Returns `store`.\"\n  1077\t  [store]\n  1078\t  (vm/check-bindings! :macro store)\n  1079\t  (doseq [entry (vals store)] (verified-tree entry))\n  1080\t  store)\n  1081\t\n  1082\t\n  1083\t(defn- invoke*\n  1084\t  \"Run one macro body. `entry` is a macro-store value (`macro-entry`),\n  1085\t   verified before anything runs. `counter` is the attempt counter, which\n  1086\t   gensyms read. `{:tree packet}` or `{:error e}`.\"\n  1087\t  [entry operands ctx counter]\n  1088\t  (let [macro-tree (verified-tree entry)\n  1089\t        macro-root (first macro-tree)\n  1090\t        params (nth (root-row macro-tree) 2)\n  1091\t        {:keys [env expected got]} (bind-arguments params operands)]\n  1092\t    (if-not env\n  1093\t      {:error {:kind :arity, :macro macro-root, :expected expected, :got got}}\n  1094\t      (let [n (volatile! 0)\n  1095\t            token (get-in ctx [:incarnation :yin.expander/token])\n  1096\t            gensym (fn [prefix]\n  1097\t                     (let [i @n]\n  1098\t                       (vswap! n inc)\n  1099\t                       (symbol (str (if (symbol? prefix) (name prefix) prefix)\n  1100\t                                    \"__\" token \"_\" counter \"_\" i))))\n  1101\t            lineage (atom [])\n  1102\t            _ (doseq [p operands] (register-lineage! lineage p))\n  1103\t            run (or (:eval ctx) bounded-row-evaluator)\n  1104\t            {:keys [value error]} (run {:macro-tree macro-tree,\n  1105\t                                        :contract (:yin.macro/contract entry),\n  1106\t                                        :env env,\n  1107\t                                        :prelude (prelude gensym lineage),\n  1108\t                                        :max-steps (get-in ctx [:guards :max-steps])})]\n  1109\t        (if error\n  1110\t          {:error (assoc error :macro macro-root)}\n  1111\t          {:tree (if (and (packet? value)\n  1112\t                          (nil? (origin-of-fn value)))\n  1113\t                   (if-some [f (lineage-origin-for lineage value)]\n  1114\t                     (with-origin-of value f)\n  1115\t                     value)\n  1116\t                   value)})))))\n  1117\t\n  1118\t\n  1119\t(def default-guards\n  1120\t  {:max-depth 100,\n  1121\t   :max-rows-per-expansion 10000,\n  1122\t   :max-rows-per-batch nil,\n  1123\t   :max-steps 100000})\n  1124\t\n  1125\t\n  1126\t(defn invoke\n  1127\t  \"Run `entry`, a macro-store value (`macro-entry`: a self-contained lambda\n  1128\t   packet and its AST contract), on `operand-trees` and return its result\n  1129\t   tree packet, unvalidated. The contract is verified first\n  1130\t   (`:contract-missing`, `:contract-mismatch`, thrown). Gensyms use\n  1310\t\n  1311\t(defn- macro-of\n  1312\t  \"The stored macro packet for an operator occurrence: a `:variable` naming\n  1313\t   a store entry that no enclosing lambda parameter shadows.\"\n  1314\t  [st operator shadow]\n  1315\t  (let [row (get (:index st) operator)]\n  1316\t    (when (and (= :variable (row-tag row))\n  1317\t               (not (contains? shadow (nth row 2))))\n  1318\t      (get (:store st) (nth row 2)))))\n  1319\t\n  1320\t\n  1321\t(defn- record-event\n  1322\t  [st event-row*]\n  1323\t  (update st :events conj event-row*))\n  1324\t\n  1325\t\n  1326\t(defn- guard-batch-rows\n  1327\t  [st]\n  1328\t  (let [limit (get-in st [:ctx :guards :max-rows-per-batch])\n  1329\t        n (count (:index st))]\n  1330\t    (when (and limit (> n limit))\n  1331\t      {:kind :row-guard, :scope :batch, :rows n})))\n  1332\t\n  1333\t\n  1334\t(defn- merge-output\n  1335\t  \"Merge a validated result packet into the working index; an address whose\n  1336\t   working body differs is an `:address-conflict`.\"\n  1337\t  [st [_ rows]]\n  1338\t  (reduce (fn [st row]\n  1339\t            (let [prior (get (:index st) (first row))]\n  1340\t              (cond (nil? prior) (assoc-in st [:index (first row)] row)\n  1341\t                    (same-value? prior row) st\n  1342\t                    :else (reduced (assoc st ::conflict (first row))))))\n  1343\t          st\n  1344\t          rows))\n  1345\t\n  1346\t\n  1347\t(declare expand-node)\n  1348\t\n  1349\t\n  1350\t(defn- output-correspondence\n  1351\t  \"The per-occurrence correspondence of the expansion's output (ruling\n  1352\t   U1): for every `:application` occurrence of output packet `tree`, at\n